Package: ff802-ucm-profile
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bernhard Steinheber <bernhard@steinheber.info>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: alsa-ucm-conf (>= 1.2.15.3), libasound2t64 (>= 1.2.15.3)
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Description: ALSA UCM profile for the RME Fireface 802 in class compliant mode
 Provides six separately selectable stereo outputs (Analog 1/2, 3/4, 5/6,
 7/8, Headphones 9/10 and 11/12) and one stereo input (Analog 1/2) of the
 original Fireface 802 (not the 802 FS) through UCM SplitPCM.
 .
 alsa-lib before 1.2.16 ignores USB-Audio/conf.d, so the profile is bound
 to the connected card by its long name (ff802-ucm-bind). The long name
 contains the USB port; a udev rule binds the card automatically whenever
 it is connected, also on a new port. With alsa-lib >= 1.2.16 no binding is
 created. No file of alsa-ucm-conf is modified.
 .
 Analog outputs 1/2 are physically confirmed; the other outputs are not yet
 verified (hardware test T2). No PipeWire or WirePlumber configuration is
 needed: WirePlumber 0.5 creates the six sinks itself.
